translated_text:
REGENT OF MUARA ENIM
PROVINCE OF SOUTH SUMATRA
REGIONAL REGULATION OF MUARA ENIM REGENCY
NUMBER 5 YEAR 2023
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF MUARA ENIM,

Considering:
a. that to guarantee the Protection of Women and Children in accordance with their dignity and to guarantee their right to life in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination and to receive Protection from violence and other violations, legal certainty is necessary;
b. that to provide legal certainty in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children and to carry out mandatory regional government affairs, regulation in the form of a Regional Regulation is necessary;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children;

In view of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 28 Year 1959 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 3 Year 1950 concerning the Establishment of Level I Region of South Sumatra and Emergency Law Number 16 Year 1955 concerning Amendment to Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 3 Year 1950 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1959 Number 70, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1814);
(2)
3. Law Number 7 Year 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3277);
4. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
5. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 Year 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 Year 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
6. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
7. Law Number 11 Year 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);
8. Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times, most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 Year 2022 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 238, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6841);
(3)
9. Government Regulation Number 78 Year 2021 concerning Special Protection for Children (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2021 Number 174, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6704);
10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 11 Year 2011 concerning Policy for Development of Child-Friendly Regency/City;
11. Regional Regulation Number 14 Year 2014 concerning Free Legal Aid (Regional Gazette of Muara Enim Regency Year 2014 Number 014);
12. Regional Regulation Number 9 Year 2020 concerning Implementation of Child-Friendly Regency (Regional Gazette Year 2020 Number 9);
13. Regional Regulation of Muara Enim Regency Number 2 Year 2022 concerning Gender Mainstreaming (Regional Gazette of Muara Enim Regency Year 2021 Number 2);

With Mutual Approval of
THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF MUARA ENIM REGENCY
and

text:
Pasal 2
Penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak berdasarkan  asas:
a. kepentingan terbaik bagi perempuan dan Anak;
b. keadilan gender dan kesetaraan gender;
c. kearifan lokal;
d. penegakan dan kepastian hukum.
e. non diskriminasi;
f. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup, dan perkembangan; g. penghargaan terhadap pendapat Anak; dan
h. penegakan dan kepastian hukum.

translated_text:
Article 2
The Implementation of Protection of Women and Children is based on the principles of:
a. the best interests of women and Children;
b. gender justice and gender equality;
c. local wisdom;
d. law enforcement and legal certainty.
e. non-discrimination;
f. the right to life, survival, and development; g. respect for the opinion of Children; and
h. law enforcement and legal certainty.

text:
Pasal 3
Peraturan Daerah ini bertujuan:
a. menjamin terpenuhinya hak perempuan dan Anak di Kabupaten;
(8)
b. sebagai pedoman bagi Daerah dalam perencanaan, kebijakan dan strategi Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;
c. melindungi dan mencegah perempuan dan Anak dari tindakan, keputusan dan kebijakan yang melanggar hak perempuan dan Anak;
d. meningkatkan peran dan nilai kearifan lokal serta peranan adat dalam Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;
e. sebagai payung hukum bagi perangkat daerah yang membidangi perlindungan perempuan dan anak dalam rangka memberi bantuan pendampingan korban perempuan dan anak.

translated_text:
Article 3
This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and Children in the Regency;
(8)
b. serve as a guideline for the Region in planning, policies and strategies for the Protection of Women and Children;
c. protect and prevent women and Children from actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of women and Children;
d. enhance the role and value of local wisdom as well as the role of customs in the Protection of Women and Children;
e. serve as a legal umbrella for regional apparatus that handle the protection of women and children in the context of providing assistance and support to women and child victims.

text:
Pasal 4
Ruang lingkup pengaturan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak  meliputi:
a. perlindungan perempuan;
b. perlindungan Anak;
c. pemenuhan hak Anak;
d. peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan;
e. sistem data gender dan Anak, data terpilah perempuan dan anak, dan penguatan kelembagaan Pengarusutamaan Gender melalui Perencanaan dan Penganggaran Responsif Gender;
f. peran serta masyarakat; dan
g. pembinaan, pengawasan, pendampingan.

translated_text:
Article 4
The scope of regulation for the Protection of Women and Children includes:
a. protection of women;
b. protection of Children;
c. fulfillment of Children's rights;
d. improvement of women's quality of life;
e. gender and Children data systems, disaggregated data on women and children, and strengthening of Gender Mainstreaming institutions through Gender Responsive Planning and Budgeting;
f. community participation; and
g. guidance, supervision, assistance.

text:
Pasal 5
( 1) Dalam rangka meningkatkan kualitas hid up perempuan, pemerintah daerah bertanggung jawab:
a. menghormati dan menjamin hak perempuan tanpa diskriminasi sesuai dengan harkat dan martabat kemanusiaan;
b. melaksanakan Pengarusutamaan Gender di Kabupaten; c. membentuk pokja Pengarusutamaan Gender di Daerah; d. meningkatkan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dalam peran, kualitas dan kemampuan dibidang (9)
1. politik;
2. hukum;
3. sosial;
4. ekonomi; dan
5. budaya.
e. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan Pemberdayaan Perempuan di Kabupaten.
(2) Tanggungjawab Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam upaya peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh perangkat daerah sesuai dengan tugas dan fungsinya.

translated_text:
Article 5
(1) In order to improve the quality of life of women, the regional government is responsible for:
a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity and worth;
b. implementing Gender Mainstreaming in the Regency; c. establishing a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region; d. enhancing Women's Empowerment in terms of role, quality and capacity in the fields of (9)
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social;
4. economy; and
5. culture.
e. strengthening and developing institutions providing Women's Empowerment services in the Regency.
(2) The responsibility of the Regency Government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

text:
Pasal 6
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam  bidang politik sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf d  angka 1 meliputi:
a. melaksanakan sosialisasi untuk meningkatkan partisipasi politik perempuan dalam pemilihan umum;
b. melaksanakan program yang mendorong tingkat keterlibatan perempuan dalam proses politik dan jabatan publik;
c. melakukan fasilitasi pengembangan diri perempuan dalam berorganisasi, berserikat dan berkumpul; dan
d. melibatkan perempuan dalam pengambilan keputusan yang menyangkut kepentingan perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 6
Efforts to increase the role, quality and capability of women in the political field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 1 include:
a. implementing socialization to increase women's political participation in general elections;
b. implementing programs that encourage the level of women's involvement in political processes and public positions;
c. facilitating the self-development of women in organizing, associating and assembling; and
d. involving women in decision-making concerning women's interests.

text:
Pasal 8
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam  biclang sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf cl  angka 3 meliputi:
a. peningkatan pengetahuan dan keterampilan untuk mendorong  pemenuhan pendidikan sesuai dengan potensi yang dimiliki;  b. peningkatan dan pemenuhan kualitas kesehatan terhaclap  perempuan;
c. peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan tentang perencanaan  keluarga mandiri, sehat dan sejahtera termasuk akses layanan  konsultasi dan pencatatan perkawinan;
d. peningkatan kesadaran perempuan terhadap dampak pernikahan  dini;
e. memfasilitasi dan mengupayakan pelestarian adat istiadat dan  pengembangan ilmu pengetahuan, teknologi, seni dan budaya untuk  kemajuan perempuan;
f. melakukan peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan perempuan  terhadap perencanaan keluarga mandiri, sehat clan sejahtera;  g. melakukan program dalam menurunkan angka kematian ibu  melahirkan; clan
h. menclorong pembentukan organisasi perempuan di Kabupaten.

translated_text:
Article 8
Efforts to increase the role, quality and capability of women in the social field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter cl number 3 include:
a. increasing knowledge and skills to encourage the fulfillment of education in accordance with existing potential;
b. increasing and fulfilling health quality for women;
c. increasing awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;
d. increasing women's awareness of the impact of early marriage;
e. facilitating and endeavoring to preserve customs and traditions and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;
f. increasing women's awareness and knowledge of independent, healthy and prosperous family planning;
g. implementing programs to reduce maternal mortality rates; and
h. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations in the Regency.

text:
Pasal 9
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam  bidang ekonomi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf d  angka 4 meliputi: (11)
a. melaksanakan program, kegiatan, pelatihan untuk peningkatan keterampilan dan keahlian perempuan dalam rangka mewujudkan peningkatan kesejahteraan perempuan;
b. fasilitasi penguatan modal usaha bagi perempuan yang memiliki ekonomi lemah;
c. pemasaran produk hasil usaha perempuan yang memiliki ekonomi lemah;
d. pelatihan pengembangan kemampuan perempuan melalui  pemberdayaan ekonomi keluarga prasejahtera; dan
e. pelatihan kewirausahaan kepada perempuan secara komprehensif.

translated_text:
Article 9
Efforts to increase the role, quality and capability of women in the economic field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 4 include: (11)
a. implementing programs, activities, training for improving the skills and expertise of women in order to realize the improvement of women's welfare;
b. facilitation of business capital strengthening for women with weak economic capacity;
c. marketing of products resulting from businesses of women with weak economic capacity;
d. training for developing women's capabilities through economic empowerment of pre-prosperous families; and
e. comprehensive entrepreneurship training for women.

text:
Pasal 10
(1) Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam upaya Perlindungan perempuan bertanggungjawab:
a. menetapkan dan menyelenggarakan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan perempuan;
b. melakukan upaya pencegahan terjadinya tindak Kekerasan terhadap perempuan termasuk tindak pidana perdagangan orang;
c. meningkatkan efektivitas layanan terhadap perempuan korban tindak Kekerasan;
d. meningkatkan upaya perlindungan terhadap tenaga kerja perempuan;
e. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan perlindungan perempuan;
f. melakukan kerjasama dengan Pemerintah, Pemerintah Daerah lainnya, pihak swasta, dunia usaha dan/atau Lembaga Swadaya Masyarakat dalam upaya pencegahan terjadinya tindak Kekerasan terhadap perempuan;
g. melibatkan peran aktif keluarga, pemuka adat, pemuka agama, masyarakat, dan lembaga dibidang perlindungan perempuan.
(12) (2) Tanggungjawab Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam upaya perlindungan  perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh  perangkat daerah sesuai dengan tugas dan fungsinya serta dapat  berkoordinasi dengan instansi terkait.

translated_text:
Article 10
(1) The Regency Government in efforts to Protect women is responsible for:
a. establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women;
b. undertaking prevention efforts against acts of Violence against women including criminal acts of human trafficking;
c. increasing the effectiveness of services for women victims of acts of Violence;
d. increasing protection efforts for female workers;
e. strengthening and developing institutions providing women's protection services;
f. conducting cooperation with the Government, other Regional Governments, private parties, business sectors and/or Non-Governmental Organizations in efforts to prevent acts of Violence against women;
g. involving the active role of families, customary leaders, religious leaders, communities, and institutions in the field of women's protection.
(12) (2) The responsibility of the Regency Government in efforts to protect women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions and may coordinate with relevant agencies.

text:
Pasal 11
Dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya tindak Kekerasan terhadap  perempuan, Pemerintah Kabupaten :
a. menyelenggarakan sosialisasi, mengenai pencegahan kekerasan  terhadap perempuan dengan mengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat,  budaya, agama dan organisasi kemasyarakatan;
b. membangun jejaring dan kerja sama dengan aparatur penegak  hukum, aparatur pemerintah, perguruan tinggi dan berbagai  Lembaga Swadaya Masyarakat yang bergerak dan/ atau peduli  terhadap perempuan dan anak korban Kekerasan;
c. menyediakan fasilitas umum yang nyaman dan aman untuk  perempuan;
d. membentuk Unit Pelayanan Teknis Daerah Perlindungan Perempuan  dan Anak serta menyediakan sekretariat Unit Pelayanan Teknis  Daerah Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak.

translated_text:
Article 11
In order to prevent acts of Violence against women, the Regency Government:
a. conducts socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. builds networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various Non-Governmental Organizations that work and/or care about women and children victims of Violence;
c. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women;
d. establishes a Regional Technical Service Unit for the Protection of Women and Children and provides a secretariat for the Regional Technical Service Unit for the Protection of Women and Children.

text:
Pasal 12
( 1) Perlindungan perempuan korban tindak Kekerasan dilaksanakan  melalui layanan terpadu.
(2) Pemberian layanan terpadu terhadap perempuan korban tindak  Kekerasan sebagiamana dimaksud pada ayat (1) menggunakan  prinsip:
a. responsif gender;
b. non diskriminasi;
(13)
c. hubungan setara dan menghormati;
d. menjaga kerahasiaan;
e. memberi rasa arnan dan nyarnan;
f. menghargai perbedaan individu;
g. tidak menghakimi;
h. menghormati pilihan dan keputusan korban;
1. peka terhadap latar belakang dan kondisi korban dan pemakaian  bahasa yang sesuai dan dimengerti oleh korban;
J. cepat dan sederhana;
k. empati; dan
1. pemenuhan hak perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 12
(1) Protection of women victims of acts of Violence is implemented through integrated services.
(2) The provision of integrated services to women victims of acts of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) uses the principles of:
a. gender responsive;
b. non-discrimination;
(13)
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of security and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
i. sensitive to the background and conditions of victims and the use of language that is appropriate and understood by victims;
j. fast and simple;
k. empathy; and
l. fulfillment of women's rights.

text:
Pasal 13
Bentuk layanan terpadu terhadap perempuan korban tindak  kekerasan meliputi:
a. penanganan pengaduan; ·
b. pelayanan kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. pendampingan korban, penegakan dan bantuan hukum; dan  e. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.

translated_text:
Article 13
The form of integrated services for women victims of violence includes:
a. complaint handling;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. victim assistance, enforcement and legal aid; and e. repatriation and social reintegration.

text:
Pasal 14
Layanan terpadu penanganan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud  dalam Pasal 13 huruf a dilaksanakan oleh:
a. Rumah Sakit, Pusat Kesehatan Masyarakat dan sarana pelayanan  kesehatan lainnya;
b. Unit Pelaksana Teknis Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;  c. Rumah Perlindungan Trauma Center,
d. Women crisis centre;
e. Badan Penasehat Pembinaan Dan Pelestarian Perkawinan;  f. Kepolisian;
g. Kejaksaan;
h. Pengadilan;
i. Kementerian Agama; dan/ atau J. Lembaga Bantuan Hukum.
{14)

translated_text:
Article 14
Integrated complaint handling services as referred to in Article 13 letter a shall be implemented by:
a. Hospitals, Community Health Centers and other health service facilities;
b. Technical Implementation Unit for the Protection of Women and Children;
c. Trauma Center Shelter,
d. Women crisis centre;
e. Advisory Board for Marriage Development and Preservation;
f. Police;
g. Prosecutor's Office;
h. Court;
i. Ministry of Religious Affairs; and/or J. Legal Aid Institution.
{14)

text:
Pasal 16
(1) Rehabilitasi kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 13  huruf b merupakan upaya yang meliputi aspek:
a. promotif;
b. preventif;
C. kuratif; dan
d. rehabilitatif.
(2) Rehabilitasi kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  dilakukan secara komprehensif, dapat diakses 24 (dua puluh  empat) jam, berkualitas dan dilakukan sesuai dengan standar  pelayanan kesehatan.
(15) (3) Perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan dan anak  berhadapan dengan hukum memiliki hak terhadap pelayanan  kesehatan secara bebas biaya, meliputi:
a. pelayanan medis;
b. pelayanan medikolegal;
c. konseling psikososial; dan
d. visum.
(4) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai tata cara pelaksanaan pelayanan  kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (3) diatur dengan  Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 16
(1) Health rehabilitation as referred to in Article 13 letter b constitutes efforts that include aspects of:
a. promotive;
b. preventive;
c. curative; and
d. rehabilitative.
(2) Health rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted comprehensively, accessible 24 (twenty-four) hours, with quality and conducted in accordance with health service standards.
(15) (3) Women and children victims of acts of violence and children in conflict with the law have the right to free health services, including:
a. medical services;
b. medicolegal services;
c. psychosocial counseling; and
d. visum.
(4) Further provisions regarding the procedures for implementation of health services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 17
(1) Rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 13 huruf c  ditujukan untuk memulihkan dan mengembangkan kemampuan  terhadap perempuan korban tindak Kekerasan yang mengalami  disfungsi sosial untuk dapat melaksanakan fungsi sosialnya dalam  masyarakat secara wajar.
(2) Rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi  pelayanan:
a. motivasi dan diagnosis psikososial;
b. perawatan dan pengasuhan;
c. pelatihan vokasional dan pembinaan kewirausahaan;  d. bimbingan mental spiritual;
e. bimbingan fisik;
f. bim bing an sosial dan konseling psikososial;
g. pelayanan aksesibilitas;
h. bantuan dan asistensi sosial;
1. bimbingan resosialisasi;
